  "explanation": "<strong>Step-by-step Explanation:</strong><br><br>We can derive the recursive relationship between consecutive iterations for both outputs $X(i)$ and $Y(i)$ for $i > 0$:<br><br>1. <strong>Analyzing Output $X(i)$:</strong><br>• For $i = 1$: $X(1) = 20 + (-4) = 16 = X(0) + I(1)$<br>• For $i = 2$: $X(2) = 16 + 10 = 26 = X(1) + I(2)$<br>• For $i = 3$: $X(3) = 26 + 15 = 41 = X(2) + I(3)$<br>This gives: $X(i) = X(i - 1) + I(i)$ for $i > 0$.<br><br>2. <strong>Analyzing Output $Y(i)$:</strong><br>• For $i = 1$: $Y(1) = 20 \\times (-4) = -80 = Y(0) \\times I(1)$<br>• For $i = 2$: $Y(2) = -80 \\times 10 = -800 = Y(1) \\times I(2)$<br>• For $i = 3$: $Y(3) = -800 \\times 15 = -12000 = Y(2) \\times I(3)$<br>This gives: $Y(i) = Y(i - 1)I(i)$ for $i > 0$.<br><br>Therefore, the correct option is <strong>(A)</strong>.",
